152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 334 0 R
/E (User Management & Authentication: The system supports role-based access for Admin, Teacher, Student, and Parent users with secure JWT token authentication. Each role has specific permissions - teachers create and grade assignments while marking attendance, students submit work and track their performance, parents monitor their children's academic progress, and admins manage institutional operations including batch assignments and user accounts.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
153 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 335 0 R
/E (Academic Operations: Teachers can create assignments with file attachments \(PDF, DOC, DOCX, images up to 10MB\) and assign them to specific batches with due dates. Students submit assignments digitally with optional file uploads, and teachers grade submissions with numerical scores and written feedback. The system automatically calculates average grades as percentages, tracks submission status \(Pending, Submitted, Graded, Overdue\), and provides performance analytics through visual dashboards. Additionally, teachers mark daily attendance with four status types \(Present, Late, Absent, Excused\), and the system calculates attendance percentages and displays trends over time.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 336 0 R
/E (Dashboard & Monitoring: Role-specific dashboards provide real-time insights - students see pending assignments, grade averages, and attendance records; teachers view submission counts, pending grading tasks, and batch details; parents access consolidated data for all their children including grades, attendance, and assignments. The system includes notification mechanisms for assignment deadlines, file management for uploads/downloads, and batch management for organizing students by grade level and subject.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
